KZ2 patch 6026: the FIFO walker follows the new-form RSX JUMP (offset | 1) as well as the old one (0x20000000 | offset).

The walker decoded a JUMP only as w >> 29 == 1. The RSX also takes JUMP as (w & 0xE0000003) == 1 with target
w & 0xFFFFFFFC (RPCS3 rsx_methods.h RSX_METHOD_NEW_JUMP_CMD; read, not copied); the walker read that word as a method
header (type 0, count (w >> 18) & 0x7FF) and walked on into the words behind it, writing them into registers until a
resync (a black room in another ps3recomp port; a register the game writes only on change stays wrong). Masks kept
in one place: libs/video/gcm_fifo_word.h (new). The new form goes through the existing JUMP branch, self-JUMP park
check included; CALL takes its target with 0xFFFFFFFC and RETURN is matched with 0xFFFF0003 as RPCS3 does. The park
diagnostics (KZ3 1008 park-diag, 1009 park-trace terminator, 1025 park-scan), the 6008 command watch and the
reference rescue scans read both forms. GCM_WORD_STATS splits the jump count: jump= (old form), jumpn= (new form),
and hdr0= (method headers with count 0); a running "[words] new-form JUMPs so far" line appears once there are any.
Host test: tools/runtime/test_gcm_jump.sh. Upstream: a candidate, shared with other ps3recomp ports.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

